      "problem": "$\\int ({sech}^{2}⁡z+\\operatorname{csch}⁡z\\operatorname{coth}⁡z)\\,\\text{d}z=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}z}(\\operatorname{csch}⁡z)=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡z\\operatorname{coth}⁡z & \\,⇒\\,\\int \\operatorname{csch}⁡z\\operatorname{coth}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡z+C, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}z}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡z)={sech}^{2}⁡z & \\,⇒\\,\\int {sech}^{2}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z=\\operatorname{tanh}⁡z+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({sech}^{2}⁡z+\\operatorname{csch}⁡z\\operatorname{coth}⁡z)\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int {sech}^{2}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z+\\int \\operatorname{csch}⁡z\\operatorname{coth}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tanh}⁡z-\\operatorname{csch}⁡z+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
